  """Terrasses du Larzac covers 32 communes on the foothills of the Larzac plateau north-west of Montpellier, around Aniane, Saint-Jean-de-Fos, Jonquières and Saint-Saturnin. Its great asset is the big difference between day and night temperatures (often 20°C), because cold air flows down from the plateau. The reds are fresh, dark and mineral. AOC since 2014, it is home to the Languedoc's most famous estates: Mas de Daumas Gassac, Grange des Pères and Mas Jullien, as well as Domaine de Montcalmès and Clos du Serres.""",
