  """Montpeyroux, in the foothills of the Larzac, became the Languedoc's newest communal AOC in 2026 after nearly 30 years of campaigning. The INAO's national committee approved its specification in June 2025, and the appellation replaces the former 'Languedoc Montpeyroux' name. It covers Montpeyroux and three neighbouring communes (Arboras, Lagamas and Saint-Jean-de-Fos), about 500 ha, and is red only. The campaign was led by 35 producers, 16 of them independent estates, and began with a first INAO visit in 1996. Domaine d'Aupilhac (Sylvain Fadat), Domaine Alain Chabanon and the Castelbarry cooperative are references. The village's name comes from 'Mont Pierreux', stony mountain.""",
