  """Corbières is the largest appellation of the Languedoc, roughly 10,000 ha in the wild hills of the Aude south of Narbonne and east of Carcassonne. It is a country of Cathar castles (Quéribus, Peyrepertuse), garrigue and scattered villages, and its wines, mostly red and often led by Carignan, range from rustic to impressive. Eleven terroir zones have been identified, from the coastal Fontfroide and Sigean to the high Hautes-Corbières. The best estates include Château de Lastours, Domaine de Villemajou (Gérard Bertrand), Maxime Magnon, Domaine Ledogar and Château La Voulte-Gasparets, whose Cuvée Romain Pauc helped make the area's name.""",
