  """Minervois lies on the southern slopes of the Montagne Noire, between Narbonne and Carcassonne, in an amphitheatre facing south toward the Canal du Midi and the Aude. It takes its name from Minerve, a cliff-top village where 140 Cathars were burned in 1210. The reds, Syrah and Grenache-led, are smoother and more fragrant than Corbières. The area is divided into several zones, from the cool, high Petit Causse to the warm, lower Canal du Midi area. In June 2025 the INAO opened consultation on Cazelles, a proposed new named area (DGC).""",
